// Jest Snapshot v1, https://goo.gl/fbAQLP

exports[`component catalog (AI tutor v2) is deterministic (part of the cached prompt prefix) 1`] = `
"- Urn: The student is unsure what is drawn or what one outcome is: show the balls with their values (duplicates marked). Student: Taps balls to select a draw. Teaches: sample-space, simultaneous-draw. props: {mode?: "display"|"select"="display", selected?: string[], markDuplicates?: boolean=true, valueFn?: "product"|"sum"|"max"|"min"|"identity" | {id: "count_value", args: {value: int}}, insight?: Rich} Props rules: For drawing balls only (probability), never for functions. insight: Arabic runs in Arabic script only; a letter, a number or a formula is its own "fr" run; no LaTeX.
- OutcomeSpace: Counting outcomes or listing the values of X is wrong (ordered vs unordered pairs, a missed pair, values of the balls instead of products): show every outcome, optionally coloured by value or by an event. Student: Scans and taps outcomes; reads the count. Teaches: counting-pairs, simultaneous-draw, random-variable-values. props: {valueFn?: "product"|"sum"|"max"|"min"|"identity" | {id: "count_value", args: {value: int}}, colorBy?: "value"|"event"|"none"="none", event?: Def0, layout?: "grid"|"list"="grid", showCount?: boolean=true, highlight?: string[], markDuplicates?: boolean=true, insight?: Rich} where Def0 = {id: "any_value", args: {value: int}} | {id: "all_equal"} | {id: "value_eq", args: {valueFn?: "product"|"sum"|"max"|"min"|"identity" | {id: "count_value", args: {value: int}}, value: int}} | {id: "not", args: {event: Def0}} | {id: "and"|"or", args: {events: Def0[]}} Props rules: Set showCount false when the count is what the student must find. colorBy "value" needs valueFn; colorBy "event" needs event. insight: Arabic runs in Arabic script only; a letter, a number or a formula is its own "fr" run; no LaTeX.
- ComplementView: "au moins un" or a complement is confused: show P(E) and P(not E) as one split bar with 1 - P on its own line. Student: Toggles between the event and its complement. Teaches: complement, au-moins-un. props: {event: Def0, valueFn?: "product"|"sum"|"max"|"min"|"identity" | {id: "count_value", args: {value: int}}, direction?: "to_complement"|"from_complement"="from_complement", interactive?: boolean=true, labels?: {event: string, complement: string}} where Def0 = {id: "any_value", args: {value: int}} | {id: "all_equal"} | {id: "value_eq", args: {valueFn?: "product"|"sum"|"max"|"min"|"identity" | {id: "count_value", args: {value: int}}, value: int}} | {id: "not", args: {event: Def0}} | {id: "and"|"or", args: {events: Def0[]}}
- LawChart: After the law is known: see it as bars, check the sum is 1, then E(X), E(X²), V(X) step by step. Student: Reveals each step. Teaches: random-variable-law, expectation, variance. props: {valueFn?: "product"|"sum"|"max"|"min"|"identity" | {id: "count_value", args: {value: int}}, reveal?: ("E"|"E2"|"V")[]=[], showFormula?: boolean=true, markDuplicates?: boolean=true}
- FunctionPlot: A picture of the curve helps (shape, symmetry, behaviour at infinity) before any computation. Student: Looks, then answers the next question. Teaches: function-parity, limit-at-infinity, variation-table. props: {fn: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", domain?: number[]=[-4,4], range?: number[], shade?: {from: number, to: number, sign?: "auto"|"pos"|"neg"="auto"}, colorBySign?: boolean=false} Props rules: fn is a function id from the exercise (never a formula); domain inside where fn is defined. No markers.
- PointOnCurve: Parity is not seen: compare f(x) and f(-x) live for chosen x values, optionally against a non-even function. Student: Drags x and compares the two values. Teaches: function-parity. props: {fn: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", x0?: number=1, showMirror?: boolean=true, compareFn?: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", domain?: number[]=[-3,3], range?: number[], step?: number=0.1}
- FoldSymmetry: Parity as a picture: fold the left half of the curve over the y-axis and see whether it matches. Student: Drags the fold slider. Teaches: function-parity. props: {fn: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", compareFn?: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", domain?: number[]=[-3,3], range?: number[]}
- TangentSlope: Link the sign of f' to increasing / decreasing: a tangent with its slope as x moves. Student: Drags x and watches the slope sign. Teaches: derivative-meaning, variation-table. props: {fn: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", x0?: number=-1, domain?: number[]=[-3,3], range?: number[], step?: number=0.1, showTable?: boolean=false}
- SecantToTangent: The meaning of f' is unclear: a secant whose second point slides to the first. Student: Steps h down and compares slopes. Teaches: derivative-meaning. props: {fn: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", x0?: number=-1, hSteps?: number[]=[3,2,1,0.5,0.2,0.1,0.05,0.01], domain?: number[]=[-3,3], range?: number[]}
- LimitExplorer: A limit at infinity is wrong (value at 0 used instead, sign of e^-x, forme indéterminée): show numerator, denominator and f(x) as x grows. Student: Drags x towards infinity and reads the values. Teaches: limit-at-infinity, forme-indeterminee, exp-limits, asymptote-interpretation. props: {fn: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", numerator?: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", denominator?: "f_ex4"|"f_ex4_num"|"f_ex4_den"|"f_ex4_simplified"|"f_ex4_prime"|"sigmoid_demo"|"quot_demo"|"exp_neg"|"g_ex4_transfer", direction?: "+inf"|"-inf"="+inf", xMax?: number=10, zoom?: boolean=false, step?: number=0.5}
- PredictReveal: Ask before telling: the student predicts first, then the inner component reveals the answer. Wraps one other component. Student: Makes a prediction (or taps "show me"), then explores. Teaches: (what the inner component teaches). props: {prompt: Rich, options: ({id: string, label: Rich})[], reveal: Spec, insight?: Rich}
- CompareTwo: Two cases side by side (even vs not even, ordered vs unordered): the difference is the lesson. Wraps two components. Student: Explores both sides and compares. Teaches: (what the inner component teaches). props: {left: Spec, right: Spec, leftLabel?: Rich, rightLabel?: Rich, insight?: Rich}
- ExampleGenerator: Another example of the same rule, generated and checked by the engine (quotient rule, parity). Student: Asks for a new example and tries it. Teaches: quotient-rule, function-parity. props: {templateId: "quotient_linear"|"parity_exp", seed?: int=1}
- StepThrough: A computation in small steps with the reason for each; use after other forms did not help. Student: Reveals one step at a time. Teaches: (what the inner component teaches). props: {steps: ({text?: Rich, math?: string, why?: Rich})[]}
- NumericTwin: First choice for an unknown algebra error: replace the symbol with numbers and let the student test the rule (numeric twin before abstract explanation). Student: Picks numbers and compares both sides. Teaches: exp-rules. props: {symbol: string, template: string, compare?: string, values: number[], label?: Rich} Props rules: symbol: one lowercase letter, not e or i. template and compare: expressions in that letter only, written as on a calculator: digits, + - * / ^ ( ) and the letter, e.g. "a^2*a^3" or "1/a"; never LaTeX (no backslash, no braces), never words or sentences. values: 1 to 6 numbers where both expressions are defined. label: Arabic runs in Arabic script only; a letter, a number or a formula is its own "fr" run; no LaTeX."
`;
